# Mahal — shared data model (v1)

Reverse-engineered from the reference build (`mahall-v3.11-final`) — the WordPress
prototype used custom post types + post/user meta instead of real tables, so this
doc normalizes that into a proper relational schema. Use this as the shared
contract between the APEX admin (Wing A) and the React/Node public site (Wing B).

Sources checked: `mahall-cpt-v1.1.php`, `mahall-ai-proxy-v0.7.php`,
`mahall-v1.1` through `v1.9-additions.php`, `README.md` (REST endpoint list).

---

## Entities

### USERS
One table for everyone — admins, venue owners, and clients (B2C or B2B).

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| user_id | PK | |
| email | string, unique | login identity |
| password_hash | string | |
| role | enum: `admin`, `owner`, `client_b2c`, `client_b2b` | reference build calls this `mahall_role` |
| first_name, last_name | string | |
| company | string, nullable | only for `client_b2b` |
| industry | string, nullable | only for `client_b2b` |
| plan | enum: `free`, `featured`, `premium`, nullable | mirrors the owner's venue plan (kept on both user and venue in the prototype) |
| created_at | timestamp | |

### VENUE_CATEGORIES
Lookup table. 8 fixed values in the reference build: Heritage & cultural, Hospitality & resort,
Private & exclusive, Nature & adventure, Coastal & leisure, Urban & lifestyle,
Corporate & MICE, Entertainment & production.

| Field | Type |
|---|---|
| category_id | PK |
| name | string |
| slug | string, unique |

